WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.970
It was an era when a man lived as a warrior...

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.780
He fought, staking his life on
his faith in the sword...

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.610
The final era... the Bakumatsu.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.000
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.850
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.690
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:57.900
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.570
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.170
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:12.240
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:19.250
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.350
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:36.270
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.780
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.050
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.790
It is the 15th day of the 5th month
in the 4th year of the Keio era:

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:41.630
The Battle of Ueno begins early in the morning;
the fierce battle at the Kuro Gate rages on.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:47.640
The Shogitai's counterattack is fierce and
the Imperial Army suffers devastating losses.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.840
Also, the cannon fire from Hongo Plateau
located on the side proves ineffective

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.880
due to the vast Shinobazu Lake in front of it,
not producing any significant damage.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.990
Then send Satsuma Province's forces
to the front line of the attack at the Kuro Gate.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.960
I don't care if it gets us all killed.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.190
Will that do, Masujiro-dono?

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.490
Yes.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.840
At this rate everyone's going to be killed.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:34.320
As long as it arrives, our victory
will be just a matter of time.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:41.230
The latest weapon, supposedly arriving from
Yokohama, is the reason for Omura's confidence.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.560
Yokohama Port

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.860
We must deliver it by early afternoon,
so hurry up.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:53.660
Please take care, Oryo. If you run into
Akizuki, please give him our best.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:59.370
What about you, Miss Leader?
Why don't you come with me?

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.440
It's not the best clue but it's worth
going and checking out.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.410
Don't you want to see Yo again?

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.510
I see.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.220
I guess you weren't aware of your own feelings.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.270
What are you going to do?

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.650
I heard that Harada has joined with the Shogitai.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.230
And look at me... the only one who...
I'm so pathetic...

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.770
Next up is the man with the torn umbrella.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:04.440
Don't you look at me the wrong way
or you're going to get hurt.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:11.840
For ten years have I been unable to find
myself a job and now I'm proud of this umbrella.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.150
It's over...

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.490
Next is I, the one who hides his face.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:24.830
People think I'm a demon or thief
even when I'm suffering...

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.820
Even when I'm suffering...

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:47.140
A man of such handsomeness that I cause the
fullest moon to hide behind the clouds in shame!

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.820
A bandit in woman's clothes
or a goddess of arts and wisdom?

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.290
Some may call me a homeless or groundless.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:59.360
All are correct, for I am Shiranui-kozo!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.970
Let me play it, too.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.370
Hey, are you sure?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:12.870
I'd better take good care of a customer who's
strange enough to come so early in the morning.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.510
That wasn't very nice.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.190
And finally allow me to introduce myself!

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.630
I terrify even Nue birds and crows
and they stop dead in the sky.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.690
I'm the strongman of Adachigahara.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.860
I stare down the Heavens and grab the Earth.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.200
Here comes Kakashi no Keishin!

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.070
Here he comes!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.080
Ueno

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:06.060
I can't be... I can't be late...

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.730
Please wait, Okita-san!

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.260
Akizuki-kun!

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:16.640
I understand how you feel,
but in that condition you'll be...

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.540
I know that I'm just going to trip them up.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:28.150
I'm well aware of that much,
but please let me go, Akizuki!

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:30.320
Out of my way!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.690
If you stop me, I'll kill you!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:39.960
You...

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.390
Do you pity me?

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.270
Draw!

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.230
Akizuki!

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.120
What? Kamajiro has been acting strangely?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.300
Not again!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.330
Kamajiro Enomoto, also known as
Vice-Admiral Tateaki Enomoto,

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:56.870
had escaped along with his fleet and
headed for Tateyama one month earlier.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:03.970
Later, after Katsu convinced him, he agreed
to let part of his fleet return and all seemed well,

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:12.320
but Katsu received information that he'd secretly
made contact with the Ouetsu Reppan Alliance.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.490
Kamajiro... You...

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.590
So how are things in Ueno?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.700
Probably still in deadlock.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:31.770
It sounds like both sides are lacking
a decisive measure of attack.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:35.140
That has to be a problem.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.880
I wonder if Yojiro is also in Edo after all...

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.370
Who knows?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:45.720
I just get the feeling that both he and the
war itself are somehow being controlled by it...

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.020
You mean, controlled by the Head?

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.660
Why don't we eat now?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:00.530
I'm sure you already know what this is about.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:04.300
Our revenge is exacted.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.940
So I made the decision.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.280
Don't tell me you're...

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.540
This troupe is going to be...

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.380
I'll disband the troupe as of today.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.710
I see. Just like I thought...

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.050
Oh well, that can't be helped.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:28.300
Edo Bay

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:45.770
Armstrong breech loading cannon

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.480
This will put an end to it.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.150
In a matter of 30 minutes...

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:00.130
Fire!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.810
In an instant, the tide of war
turns in favor of the Imperial Army.

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.320
Ueno has fallen!

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:27.150
The Shogitai has lost!

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:55.480
D-don't touch me!

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.520
You died too soon, Ryo.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.860
This wouldn't have happened
if you were still alive!

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.660
The establishment of the Satsuma-Choshu
Alliance two years earlier,

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:15.600
the Eight Point Program composed at sea,
the restoration of imperial rule.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:17.900
These were to be the keys
to the door to the modern age,

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.340
which Ryoma Sakamoto had opened
literally at the cost of his life.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:26.950
However, this was what happened
after the bloodless handover of Edo Castle.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:08.190
The battle was over when the rain stopped.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.710
Kyunosuke! Where are you?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.380
Kyunosuke!

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:35.620
Kyunosuke Masumichi, who dashed down
the Tokai Road with Yamaoka

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:42.720
in order to realize the meeting
with Saigo for Katsu, died at Ueno.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.420
He was 28 years old.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:14:01.140
<i>THE SOUND OF ARROWS IN THE AIR CEASED.</i>
<i>ALL THAT REMAINS IS THE SCENT</i>
<i>OF THE MOUNTAIN CHERRY BLOSSOMS.</i>
<i>KAISHU KATSU</i>

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:07.950
This famed tactician, the "Fire-Breathing Daruma"
who put an end to Battle of Ueno in a single day

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:11.780
and who successfully brought victory
to the Imperial Army,

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:16.420
was also assassinated the following year.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.920
I have a favor to ask of you, Akizuki.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:48.190
I want you to fight me again.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:53.390
But I don't want you to hold back
like the last time.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.130
Back then I didn't hold back on you, either.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.890
He must be hiding somewhere around here.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.830
Okita and that other one.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.440
Excellent. You've come far.

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:42.880
Thank you, sir.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:47.380
It is I who should be saying that. Thank you.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:52.950
Okita-san!

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:56.820
I'll go get a doctor!

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:16.440
I found you, Okita! Get him!

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:24.440
Just like we promised, we're going to
put your head next to Kondo's!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:28.960
You may be the leader, but look at you now!
You're nothing more than a stray cat.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.260
No, you're less than a sewer rat!

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.470
Akizuki...

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:26.840
I bet that black cat is here again.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.190
Yes, it's here.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:49.470
Akizuki, if you ever see Toshi, please tell him...

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:56.540
Tell him I'll go ahead of him... but I'll be waiting
for him with Commander Kondo.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:32.470
<i>SOJI OKITA DIED AT AGE 27</i>

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.620
I didn't make it in time...

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.720
Oryo...

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:17.690
Who are you?

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:24.990
I'm Sotetsu Ibaragi. I met you once when I went
to see Sakamoto-sensei in Kyoto.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.270
If I remember correctly you write the script.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:33.130
Just to kill some time. But now
I work with a performance troupe.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:35.470
Could that be the one from Yokohama?

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:39.140
Actually I have an urgent favor to ask of you.

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:50.260
Kobako, Benimaru, come, you two.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:51.450
Okay...

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:00.530
Oryo-san?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.040
IF FLOWER AND WATER STAY STILL,
THEY WILL BE SEPARATED BY DARKNESS
- SOJI OKITA

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.040
Th-this is...

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:12.210
A new story written by the master?!

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.050
I see.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.750
So you couldn't meet Akizuki-sama.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:29.990
So I want you to tell Yo something for me.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:34.600
His words... The words of Ryoma Sakamoto.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:38.700
That's right. I should've done so from the start.

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:46.180
I don't know why, but I can smell
the same thing from you and Yo...

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:52.120
What?!

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:53.490
Nakaiya is still alive?!

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.360
That's impossible!

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.490
Let me see it!

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:03.860
Now...

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:05.390
In other words...

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:10.770
We're going to perform once again.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:15.770
Not only that, the stage is in Edo.
So that means the master is also in Edo.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.940
Akizuki, too.

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:25.310
I can smell the same thing from you and Yo...

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:28.120
Leader!

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:29.590
Leader!

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:34.600
Everyone, get ready right away!

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:38.470
Here comes another revenge drama
of the Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe.

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:40.970
Our next performance is going to be in Edo!

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.560
Yeah!

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>UENO FALLS</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:48.230
EPISODE 11
THE TROUPE
AT A PROVISIONAL
STAGE AGAIN

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:37.450
Come one, come all!

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:39.120
We're the Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe!

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:42.360
We received very favorable reviews
at the Ushioza in Yokohama,

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:45.300
and now we're back with
our new performance titled

00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:50.400
"The Mysterious Tale of the
Ghost-Sealing Moontear Assassin"!

00:23:48.230 --> 00:24:02.580
THE TROUPE
AT A PROVISIONAL
STAGE AGAIN

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:53.040
We'll be performing two nights in a row.

00:23:53.200 --> 00:24:00.280
Bring your friends and neighbors
and come see us!
